            <END-TO-END-PROTECTION-SET>
              <SHORT-NAME>ReferenceCar_ChecksumCounter</SHORT-NAME>
              <DESC>
                <L-2 L="EN">The checksum and counter protection of the reference car's frames, written in AUTOSAR's end-to-end vocabulary. None of it is an AUTOSAR E2E profile (category LIONDRIVER_TOYOTA_CHECKSUM8 is not a standard category). WP-S-05 §12.3: on the reference car end-to-end protection in the usual sense (checksum, counter and timeout together) exists only on the camera's PCS frames. For comparison, WP-S-05 §12.5: Volkswagen MQB uses CRC-8H2F with a data ID per counter value, the AUTOSAR E2E profile 2 pattern; no such vehicle is configured</L-2>
              </DESC>
              <END-TO-END-PROTECTIONS>
                <END-TO-END-PROTECTION>
                  <SHORT-NAME>SPEED</SHORT-NAME>
                  <DESC>
                    <L-2 L="EN">Not an AUTOSAR E2E profile. Toyota 8-bit additive checksum: the low byte of the sum of the identifier bytes, the length and the data bytes (toyota.h toyota_compute_checksum), in the last byte; the identifier enters the sum like an AUTOSAR data ID. No counter. Checked by: not checked by the item.</L-2>
                  </DESC>
                  <ADMIN-DATA>
                    <SDGS>
                      <SDG GID="LionDriver.Source">
                        <SD GID="workProduct">WP-S-05</SD>
                        <SD GID="clause">§5, §12.3, §12.5</SD>
                        <SD GID="path">opendbc_repo/opendbc/safety/modes/toyota.h</SD>
                      </SDG>
                    </SDGS>
                  </ADMIN-DATA>
                  <END-TO-END-PROFILE>
                    <CATEGORY>LIONDRIVER_TOYOTA_CHECKSUM8</CATEGORY>
                    <DATA-IDS>
                      <DATA-ID>180</DATA-ID>
                    </DATA-IDS>
                    <DATA-LENGTH>64</DATA-LENGTH>
                    <CRC-OFFSET>56</CRC-OFFSET>
                  </END-TO-END-PROFILE>
                  <END-TO-END-PROTECTION-I-SIGNAL-I-PDUS>
                    <END-TO-END-PROTECTION-I-SIGNAL-I-PDU>
                      <DATA-OFFSET>0</DATA-OFFSET>
                      <I-SIGNAL-GROUP-REF DEST="I-SIGNAL-GROUP">/LionDriver/Communication/SPEED_Group</I-SIGNAL-GROUP-REF>
                      <I-SIGNAL-I-PDU-REF DEST="I-SIGNAL-I-PDU">/LionDriver/Communication/SPEED_IPdu</I-SIGNAL-I-PDU-REF>
                    </END-TO-END-PROTECTION-I-SIGNAL-I-PDU>
                  </END-TO-END-PROTECTION-I-SIGNAL-I-PDUS>
                </END-TO-END-PROTECTION>
                <END-TO-END-PROTECTION>
                  <SHORT-NAME>STEERING_LTA</SHORT-NAME>
                  <DESC>
                    <L-2 L="EN">Not an AUTOSAR E2E profile. Toyota 8-bit additive checksum: the low byte of the sum of the identifier bytes, the length and the data bytes (toyota.h toyota_compute_checksum), in the last byte; the identifier enters the sum like an AUTOSAR data ID. 6-bit counter COUNTER. Checked by: written by openpilot on the SoC; not checked by the panda (WP-S-05 §12.3 H2); the EPS, assumed (WP-S-05 OI-9).</L-2>
                  </DESC>
                  <ADMIN-DATA>
                    <SDGS>
                      <SDG GID="LionDriver.Source">
                        <SD GID="workProduct">WP-S-05</SD>
                        <SD GID="clause">§5, §12.3, §12.5</SD>
                        <SD GID="path">opendbc_repo/opendbc/safety/modes/toyota.h</SD>
                      </SDG>
                    </SDGS>
                  </ADMIN-DATA>
                  <END-TO-END-PROFILE>
                    <CATEGORY>LIONDRIVER_TOYOTA_CHECKSUM8</CATEGORY>
                    <DATA-IDS>
                      <DATA-ID>401</DATA-ID>
                    </DATA-IDS>
                    <DATA-LENGTH>64</DATA-LENGTH>
